  "description": "Songs from the Big Chair is the second studio album by the English pop rock band Tears for Fears, released in the UK on 1 March 1985 by Phonogram Records and Mercury Records, followed by a US release on 11 March 1985. The follow-up to the band's successful debut album, The Hurting (1983), Songs from the Big Chair marked a departure from that album's dark, introspective style, featuring a more mainstream, glossy sound, with sophisticated production values, increased guitar use, and diverse stylistic influences, while Roland Orzabal and Ian Stanley's lyrics reflected socially and politically conscious themes.",
